1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,676
What can an elephant's trunk do?

2
00:00:02,836 --> 00:00:03,896
Is it a nose?

3
00:00:03,936 --> 00:00:04,746
A hand?

4
00:00:04,786 --> 00:00:05,869
A shower?

5
00:00:06,119 --> 00:00:07,269
I'm Milo.

6
00:00:07,309 --> 00:00:09,042
Let's find out together!

7
00:00:09,212 --> 00:00:12,252
Welcome to The Animated Zoo, friends!

8
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:15,233
Today we fly to the sunny savanna.

9
00:00:15,403 --> 00:00:16,373
Here we are!

10
00:00:16,413 --> 00:00:18,277
Look who is waiting for us.

11
00:00:18,438 --> 00:00:19,878
This is Tumble.

12
00:00:19,918 --> 00:00:22,208
Tumble is a baby elephant.

13
00:00:22,378 --> 00:00:24,418
And this is Tumble's mama.

14
00:00:24,458 --> 00:00:25,724
Hello, Mama!

15
00:00:25,894 --> 00:00:28,636
Look at Tumble's long, bendy trunk.

16
00:00:28,806 --> 00:00:30,671
A trunk is a nose.

17
00:00:30,831 --> 00:00:32,641
And it is an upper lip, too.

18
00:00:32,681 --> 00:00:33,866
All in one!

19
00:00:34,026 --> 00:00:35,316
Where is your nose?

20
00:00:35,356 --> 00:00:37,046
Can you touch your nose?

21
00:00:38,196 --> 00:00:41,077
At the tip of the trunk
are two little holes.

22
00:00:41,237 --> 00:00:43,317
An elephant breathes through them.

23
00:00:43,357 --> 00:00:44,910
Sniff, sniff!

24
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,250
Sniff, sniff!

25
00:00:46,290 --> 00:00:48,412
Tumble smells something yummy.

26
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:52,148
An elephant uses its
trunk to smell its food.

27
00:00:52,318 --> 00:00:54,438
It can even smell water from far,

28
00:00:54,478 --> 00:00:55,647
far away!

29
00:00:55,817 --> 00:00:58,711
So, is a trunk a nose, or a tail?

30
00:01:02,261 --> 00:01:03,051
A nose!

31
00:01:03,091 --> 00:01:05,200
A very, very long nose.

32
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:07,070
Now Tumble is hungry.

33
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:08,450
Look, a fruit!

34
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:11,022
A trunk is like a hand, too.

35
00:01:11,182 --> 00:01:14,131
It can grab, hold, pick up and reach.

36
00:01:14,391 --> 00:01:15,931
Yum, yum, yum!

37
00:01:15,971 --> 00:01:17,630
Can you munch like Tumble?

38
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,220
Here comes Mama.

39
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:21,729
Her trunk is very, very strong.

40
00:01:21,889 --> 00:01:24,149
It can lift a big, heavy log.

41
00:01:24,189 --> 00:01:25,464
Up it goes!

42
00:01:25,624 --> 00:01:28,212
And a trunk is very gentle, too.

43
00:01:28,382 --> 00:01:31,234
It can pick up one tiny piece of straw.

44
00:01:31,404 --> 00:01:33,494
So strong, and so gentle.

45
00:01:33,534 --> 00:01:34,724
What a nose!

46
00:01:34,884 --> 00:01:37,465
There are no bones inside a trunk.

47
00:01:37,635 --> 00:01:40,425
So it can bend this way, and that way!

48
00:01:40,595 --> 00:01:42,885
Can you wiggle your arm like a trunk?

49
00:01:42,925 --> 00:01:44,485
Wiggle, wiggle!

50
00:01:44,645 --> 00:01:46,495
That is two trunk jobs.

51
00:01:46,535 --> 00:01:47,565
One, smell.

52
00:01:47,605 --> 00:01:48,847
Two, grab.

53
00:01:49,017 --> 00:01:50,637
Phew, it is hot!

54
00:01:50,677 --> 00:01:53,173
Tumble and Mama walk into the river.

55
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:54,803
Time for a drink.

56
00:01:54,843 --> 00:01:56,572
Watch Mama's trunk!

57
00:01:56,792 --> 00:02:00,222
She sucks the water up
into her trunk. Slurp!

58
00:02:00,392 --> 00:02:02,062
Does the water go all the way up her

59
00:02:02,102 --> 00:02:04,669
nose? Yes, or no?

60
00:02:08,219 --> 00:02:11,366
No! The water only goes
part of the way up.

61
00:02:11,526 --> 00:02:13,985
Then she curls her trunk to her mouth,

62
00:02:14,145 --> 00:02:15,865
and blows the water in!

63
00:02:15,905 --> 00:02:17,849
Glug, glug, glug.

64
00:02:18,019 --> 00:02:20,599
So a trunk is not like a straw.

65
00:02:20,639 --> 00:02:22,884
It carries the water to the mouth.

66
00:02:23,044 --> 00:02:25,084
Now it is Tumble's turn.

67
00:02:25,124 --> 00:02:27,091
His trunk is still short.

68
00:02:27,251 --> 00:02:31,128
Baby elephants are clumsy
with their trunks at first.

69
00:02:31,358 --> 00:02:32,408
Oops! Splash!

70
00:02:32,448 --> 00:02:34,468
The water goes everywhere.

71
00:02:34,628 --> 00:02:36,538
But Tumble keeps trying.

72
00:02:36,578 --> 00:02:38,546
Little by little, he learns.

73
00:02:38,736 --> 00:02:40,686
Can you slurp like an elephant?

74
00:02:40,726 --> 00:02:42,278
Slurp, slurp!

75
00:02:42,448 --> 00:02:46,518
A baby elephant drinks his
mama's milk with his mouth.

76
00:02:46,688 --> 00:02:49,421
So he does not need a long trunk yet.

77
00:02:49,581 --> 00:02:52,041
Now Mama fills her trunk again.

78
00:02:52,081 --> 00:02:53,366
What will she do?

79
00:02:53,526 --> 00:02:55,106
Whoosh! A shower!

80
00:02:55,146 --> 00:02:57,439
She sprays water all over her back.

81
00:02:57,609 --> 00:03:02,051
Elephants squirt cool water
over their bodies to keep cool.

82
00:03:02,211 --> 00:03:04,181
Tumble wants a shower too.

83
00:03:04,221 --> 00:03:06,025
Ready, steady, spray!

84
00:03:06,195 --> 00:03:08,185
Can you spray like an elephant?

85
00:03:08,225 --> 00:03:09,681
Whoosh, whoosh!

86
00:03:09,851 --> 00:03:12,071
Now we have four trunk jobs.

87
00:03:12,111 --> 00:03:13,191
Three, drink.

88
00:03:13,231 --> 00:03:14,726
Four, spray.

89
00:03:14,896 --> 00:03:18,241
Now Tumble wades into
the deep, deep water.

90
00:03:18,461 --> 00:03:20,950
Deeper, and deeper, and deeper.

91
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,460
Where did Tumble go?

92
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,827
Can you see him?

93
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:27,983
Peekaboo! There is the tip of his trunk.

94
00:03:28,143 --> 00:03:31,572
An elephant can use its
trunk like a snorkel.

95
00:03:31,732 --> 00:03:33,492
The tip stays up in the air,

96
00:03:33,532 --> 00:03:35,047
so he can breathe.

97
00:03:35,207 --> 00:03:38,611
Only the tip of the
trunk is above the water.

98
00:03:38,771 --> 00:03:40,311
Breathe in through your nose.

99
00:03:40,351 --> 00:03:41,161
And out.

100
00:03:41,201 --> 00:03:42,351
Can you do it?

101
00:03:42,521 --> 00:03:44,841
Tumble walks along under the water.

102
00:03:44,881 --> 00:03:46,345
Bubble, bubble!

103
00:03:46,515 --> 00:03:48,175
Let's count his bubbles.

104
00:03:48,215 --> 00:03:49,668
One, two, three!

105
00:03:49,838 --> 00:03:51,278
And out he comes.

106
00:03:51,318 --> 00:03:52,870
Drip, drip, drip!

107
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,120
Tumble flaps his big ears.

108
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,070
Flap, flap, flap!

109
00:03:57,230 --> 00:03:59,060
What did Tumble breathe with?

110
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:01,150
His trunk, or his tail?

111
00:04:04,690 --> 00:04:05,570
His trunk!

112
00:04:05,610 --> 00:04:07,158
Just like a snorkel.

113
00:04:07,318 --> 00:04:08,908
The sun goes down.

114
00:04:08,948 --> 00:04:11,030
Tumble walks home with Mama.

115
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,740
Tumble is tired.

116
00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:14,668
He comes close to Mama.

117
00:04:14,828 --> 00:04:18,619
Mama reaches out her trunk,
and strokes him gently.

118
00:04:18,819 --> 00:04:21,751
Elephants stroke each
other with their trunks.

119
00:04:21,911 --> 00:04:23,331
It is like a hug.

120
00:04:23,371 --> 00:04:24,735
A trunk hug!

121
00:04:24,935 --> 00:04:28,021
Can you give yourself a big hug? Squeeze!

122
00:04:28,191 --> 00:04:30,581
Tumble feels warm and happy.

123
00:04:30,761 --> 00:04:31,931
Five, snorkel.

124
00:04:31,971 --> 00:04:33,001
Six, hug.

125
00:04:33,041 --> 00:04:34,899
Six trunk jobs!

126
00:04:35,059 --> 00:04:37,584
One nose, six jobs. Wow!

127
00:04:37,744 --> 00:04:39,971
Time to remember what we learned!

128
00:04:40,141 --> 00:04:41,641
Is a trunk a nose?

129
00:04:41,681 --> 00:04:43,094
Yes, or no?

130
00:04:46,444 --> 00:04:48,474
Yes! A nose and an upper lip,

131
00:04:48,514 --> 00:04:49,568
all in one.

132
00:04:49,738 --> 00:04:51,888
Are there bones inside a trunk?

133
00:04:51,928 --> 00:04:53,386
Yes, or no?

134
00:04:56,736 --> 00:04:57,946
No bones!

135
00:04:57,986 --> 00:05:00,049
It bends this way and that way.

136
00:05:00,209 --> 00:05:02,809
What does Tumble use as a snorkel?

137
00:05:04,559 --> 00:05:05,827
His trunk!

138
00:05:05,987 --> 00:05:07,857
One nose, six jobs.

139
00:05:07,897 --> 00:05:09,142
Let's count them!

140
00:05:09,302 --> 00:05:11,153
Smell, grab, drink,

141
00:05:11,323 --> 00:05:13,252
spray, snorkel, hug!

142
00:05:13,422 --> 00:05:14,892
Good night, Tumble.

143
00:05:14,932 --> 00:05:16,393
Good night, Mama.

144
00:05:16,623 --> 00:05:18,843
Thank you for learning with me, friends.

145
00:05:18,883 --> 00:05:20,482
See you at the zoo!

